Cascading auto-discharge: discharge creates new obligations that also need discharging

SCENARIO: Database transaction pattern
  connect() → Connection[connected!]
  begin()   → Transaction[in_transaction!]  (consumes connected)
  commit()  → Connection[connected!]        (consumes in_transaction, CREATES connected!)
  close()   → void                          (consumes connected)

CURRENT LIMITATION (measured 2026-10-13):
  [!] is refused on any tor with output — commit's `-> *Connection<connected!>`
  hits error[KORU083] "[!] annotation requires a void tor" (also green-pinned
  by 330_037 / 330_132). The cascade scenario cannot even be declared today.

REQUIRED CHANGES:
  1. Allow [!] on single-output events (not just void)
  2. When discharging a producing event, track new obligations from output
  3. Run auto-discharge iteratively until no obligations remain

USER BENEFIT:
  Write only the happy path, compiler handles cleanup cascade:
    ~connect() | connected _ |>
        begin(conn: _.conn) | begun _ |>
            do_work(tx: _.tx) | done _ |> _

  Compiler auto-inserts: commit(tx) then close(conn)

Re-spelled to current grammar 2026-10-13 (bare returns); fails at the real
wall (KORU083) instead of PARSE003 on dead single-branch-union spelling.
